{"units": [{"id": "peitho-quote20", "translation": "unless you are persuaded by my words"}, {"id": "peitho-quote21", "translation": "persuaded by such oracles of Loxias"}, {"id": "peitho-quote22", "translation": "persuaded through the beacon-watchers"}, {"id": "peitho-quote23", "translation": "I will obey you in these words"}, {"id": "peitho-quote24", "translation": "not to trust friends"}, {"id": "peitho-quote25", "translation": "trusting in these things I will go"}, {"id": "peitho-quote26", "translation": "trusting in the strong, harsh commanders"}, {"id": "peitho-quote27", "translation": "not trusting in fortune"}, {"id": "peitho-quote28", "translation": "trusting in strength"}, {"id": "peitho-quote29", "translation": "Must we trust such oracles? And if I do not trust, the deed must still be done."}, {"id": "peitho-quote30", "translation": "trusting in justice"}, {"id": "peitho-quote31", "translation": "and I trust in Zeus"}, {"id": "peitho-quote32", "translation": "I sent them, whom I trust not to wander from the path"}, {"id": "peitho-quote33", "translation": "I trust that with justice he will come, the fire-bearer lightning"}, {"id": "peitho-quote34", "translation": "I trust that he who has the head that opposes Zeus will be struck"}, {"id": "peitho-quote35", "translation": "trusting to revere the spear he holds more than the god"}, {"id": "peitho-quote36", "translation": "to trust that the same deity will always guide fortune"}, {"id": "peitho-quote37", "translation": "I trust, and my father sends aid from the tomb"}, {"id": "peitho-quote38", "translation": "obey"}, {"id": "peitho-quote39", "translation": "obey the women"}, {"id": "peitho-quote40", "translation": "obey, leaving this wagon-borne throne"}, {"id": "peitho-quote41", "translation": "obey and let it be done"}, {"id": "peitho-quote42", "translation": "obey me, obey, and share the toil"}, {"id": "peitho-word1", "translation": "I was persuading"}, {"id": "peitho-word2", "translation": "I trust"}, {"id": "peitho-word3", "translation": "I persuaded"}, {"id": "peitho-word4", "translation": "I obeyed"}, {"id": "peitho-word5", "translation": "I obeyed"}, {"id": "peitho-word6", "translation": "I will persuade"}, {"id": "peitho-word7", "translation": "I am persuaded, I was persuaded, I will be persuaded"}, {"id": "peitho-word8", "translation": "I obey, I obeyed, I will obey"}, {"id": "peitho-word9", "translation": "you persuade M"}, {"id": "peitho-word10", "translation": "persuade him"}, {"id": "peitho-word11", "translation": "having understood within her mind, she will receive the word"}, {"id": "peitho-word12", "translation": "I obeyed"}, {"id": "peitho-word13", "translation": "having obeyed"}, {"id": "peitho-word14", "translation": "having been persuaded"}, {"id": "peitho-word15", "translation": "trusting"}, {"id": "peitho-word16", "translation": "having obeyed"}, {"id": "peitho-word17", "translation": "Plouto"}, {"id": "peitho-word18", "translation": "I obeyed"}, {"id": "peitho-word19", "translation": "persuading"}, {"id": "peitho-word20", "translation": "I am persuaded"}, {"id": "peitho-word21", "translation": "obey"}, {"id": "peitho-word22", "translation": "obey"}, {"id": "peitho-word23", "translation": "obey"}, {"id": "peitho-word24", "translation": "to obey"}, {"id": "peitho-word25", "translation": "I have been persuaded"}, {"id": "peitho-word26", "translation": "trust"}, {"id": "peitho-word27", "translation": "seek"}, {"id": "peitho-word28", "translation": "seek"}, {"id": "peitho-word29", "translation": "trust"}, {"id": "peitho-word30", "translation": "trust"}, {"id": "peitho-word31", "translation": "I was persuaded"}, {"id": "peitho-word32", "translation": "I trust"}, {"id": "peitho-word33", "translation": "I obeyed"}, {"id": "peitho-word34", "translation": "he goes. Who then would obey these things?"}, {"id": "peitho-word35", "translation": "he would obey"}, {"id": "peitho-word36", "translation": "he would obey. Eum. 794: obey me, not to bear it grievously"}, {"id": "peitho-word37", "translation": "M obey"}, {"id": "peitho-word38", "translation": "heavy is the doom of not obeying"}, {"id": "peitho-word39", "translation": "M to obey"}, {"id": "peitho-word40", "translation": "to obey"}, {"id": "peitho-word41", "translation": "to obey"}, {"id": "peitho-word42", "translation": "obey"}, {"id": "peitho-word43", "translation": "obey"}, {"id": "peitho-word44", "translation": "obey"}, {"id": "peitho-word45", "translation": "obey"}, {"id": "peitho-word46", "translation": "obey"}, {"id": "peitho-word47", "translation": "obey"}, {"id": "peitho-word48", "translation": "obey"}, {"id": "peitho-word49", "translation": "obey me, obey"}, {"id": "peitho-word50", "translation": "to leave"}, {"id": "peitho-word51", "translation": "leaving"}, {"id": "peitho-word52", "translation": "to leave"}, {"id": "peitho-word53", "translation": "leaving"}, {"id": "peitho-suada-orth1", "translation": "persuasion"}, {"id": "peitho-suada-def1", "translation": "persuasion, inducement"}, {"id": "peitho-suada-def2", "translation": "Peitho, goddess of persuasion"}, {"id": "peitho-suada-note1", "translation": "wrongly for πευθοῖ [inquiry], which Scaliger restored."}, {"id": "peitho-suada-note2", "translation": "μολπάν [song] corrected in M, which the scholiast read. Thus Bothius for ἀλκὰν [strength]. πειθώ μολπᾶν [persuasion of songs] he calls confidence in the songs, because he hopes that his auguries will be fulfilled. The scholiast rendered the sense correctly, although he wrongly took the accusative πειθώ [persuasion] as nominative, for πείθει γάρ με ἡ παρὰ θεῶν πίστις μέλπειν καὶ λέγειν ὅτι εὐ πράξουσιν οἱ Ἀτρείδαι ὅσον ἀπὸ τοῦ σημείου [the trust from the gods persuades me to sing and say that the Atreidae will fare well, as far as from the sign]."}, {"id": "peitho-suada-note3", "translation": "about which see what has been collected in Thes. vol. 6 p. 665."}, {"id": "peitho-suada-note4", "translation": "Θανάτου [of Death]"}, {"id": "peitho-suada-quote1", "translation": "with honey-tongued charms of persuasion"}, {"id": "peitho-suada-quote2", "translation": "by persuasion of what message do you sacrifice, sent around?"}, {"id": "peitho-suada-quote3", "translation": "for now deceitful persuasion is at its height"}, {"id": "peitho-suada-quote4", "translation": "for still from the gods breathes persuasion of songs, strength innate, life"}, {"id": "peitho-suada-quote5", "translation": "and wretched Peitho forces"}, {"id": "peitho-suada-quote6", "translation": "if the reverence of Peitho is holy to you"}, {"id": "peitho-suada-quote7", "translation": "I love the eyes of Peitho"}, {"id": "peitho-suada-quote8", "translation": "and may Peitho follow"}, {"id": "peitho-suada-quote9", "translation": "Desire, to whom nothing is denied, with enchanting Peitho"}, {"id": "peitho-suada-quote10", "translation": "and Peitho alone of the gods stands apart"}, {"id": "peitho-suada-word1", "translation": "inquiry"}, {"id": "peitho-suada-word2", "translation": "song"}, {"id": "peitho-suada-word3", "translation": "strength. persuasion of songs"}, {"id": "peitho-suada-word4", "translation": "persuasion"}, {"id": "peitho-suada-word5", "translation": "the trust from the gods persuades me to sing and say that the Atreidae will fare well, as far as from the sign"}, {"id": "peitho-suada-word6", "translation": "Peitho"}, {"id": "peitho-suada-word7", "translation": "of Death"}, {"id": "peira-conatus-orth1", "translation": "attempt"}, {"id": "peira-conatus-def1", "translation": "attempt"}, {"id": "peira-conatus-quote1", "translation": "the attempt of such a man must be well guarded against"}, {"id": "peira-conatus-quote2", "translation": "did a footman or sailor, wretched, make this attempt?"}, {"id": "peira-cuspis-orth1", "translation": "point, edge"}, {"id": "peira-cuspis-def1", "translation": "point, edge"}]}